# CIDR (Classless Inter-Domain Routing)

CIDR is used to define:
- Network size
- IP address range
- Number of hosts

Format:
IP_Address/Prefix

Example:
10.0.0.0/16

- 10.0.0.0 → Network Address
- /16 → First 16 bits are network bits

## Common CIDR Ranges

| CIDR | Total IPs | Usable IPs |
|------|------------|-------------|
| /24 | 256 | 251 |
| /25 | 128 | 123 |
| /26 | 64 | 59 |
| /27 | 32 | 27 |
| /28 | 16 | 11 |

Azure reserves 5 IPs in every subnet.

