# VNet and Subnet

## VNet
Virtual Network in Azure.

Example:
10.0.0.0/16

Range:
10.0.0.0 → 10.0.255.255

VNet acts as a private network in the cloud.

---

## Subnet

Subnet is a smaller network inside the VNet.

Example:

| Subnet Name | CIDR | Range |
|-------------|------|--------|
| WebSubnet | 10.0.1.0/24 | 10.0.1.0 - 10.0.1.255 |
| AppSubnet | 10.0.2.0/24 | 10.0.2.0 - 10.0.2.255 |
| DBSubnet | 10.0.3.0/24 | 10.0.3.0 - 10.0.3.255 |

## Important Rules
- Subnets must not overlap
- Subnets must be inside VNet range

Correct:
10.0.1.0/24
10.0.2.0/24

Wrong:
10.0.1.0/24
10.0.1.128/25

(Overlapping subnet)

